---
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import example from './client-environment.json';
---
<div class="comparison">
    <section aria-labelledby="client-defect">
        <p class="label">01 / The defect</p>
        <h3 id="client-defect">Private configuration in client code</h3>
        <Code code={example.broken.trimEnd()} lang="js" title="search.js" />
        <p>A client module reads a server value. Making a secret public does not fix the boundary.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="client-correction">
        <p class="label">02 / The correction</p>
        <h3 id="client-correction">Keep the private work on the server</h3>
        <Code code={example.corrected.trimEnd()} lang="js" title="search.js" />
        <p>The client names a public route. Its server implementation owns the private configuration.</p>
    </section>
</div>
<details>
    <summary>Read the captured diagnostic</summary>
    <p>gspot plugin {example.version}, ESLint 9.39.5, JavaScript module, default rule options.</p>
    <Code code={`search.js:2:25  ${example.findings[0].ruleId}\n${example.findings[0].message}`} lang="text" />
    <p>The corrected module produces zero findings from this rule. This example checks the boundary,
        not the implementation of an API route.</p>
</details>
<p><a href="/guides/client-environment/">Run the client-environment example →</a></p>
<style>
    .comparison { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 32px; }
    .comparison section { min-width: 0; }
    .label { color: var(--sl-color-text-accent); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 600; }
    h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 8px; }
    details { margin-block: 24px; }
    @media (max-width: 45rem) { .comparison { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 16px; } }
</style>
